## Summary

| quantity | value |
|---|---|
| positions with a complete ABBA quartet | **120** |
| median ratio (v3 / built-in), time per identical node budget | **0.937** |
| 2.5th / 97.5th percentile of the per-position ratio | 0.828 / 1.083 |
| positions where v3 is SLOWER (ratio > 1) | 16 of 120 |
| per-position spread (max/min ratio) | **1.48x** |
| positions where both arms reported the SAME node count | 0 of 120 |

**How to read this:** a median ratio near 1.0 means the v3 path costs about the same as the built-in
evaluation per unit of work on real positions — the bench's 21.46 %% v3 share does not translate into a
real-position penalty or benefit of that size. The per-position spread is the number that matters for any
patch claim: a patch smaller than that spread is not measurable on this sample.
